#
# DeepRoot versioning (Linux-inspired)
# Format: MAJOR.PATCHLEVEL.SUBLEVEL[-EXTRAVERSION]
#
# MAJOR      — ABI break (0 = pre-stable, 1 = stable)
# PATCHLEVEL — one feature *series* (land slowly; one series = one theme)
# SUBLEVEL   — fixes / polish / staged landings *inside* that series
# EXTRAVERSION — optional: -rcN, -dirty
#
# First line above is the CURRENT release. Lines below are the full roadmap.
#
# Policy (1.x through 1.50 → 2.0):
#   - DeepRoot-native capability ABI — NOT Linux/POSIX binary compatible.
#   - Prefer additive syscalls; note any calling-convention break in the series.
#   - **Slow the version clock:** do NOT mint a new PATCHLEVEL for every feature
#     chunk. Prefer several SUBLEVEL tags while a theme is still growing.
#   - Do not mint a new SUBLEVEL for every commit; finish a chunk, then release.
#   - Shell stays DeepRoot-native (learn from xv6/BusyBox structure; do NOT port bash).
#   - **Infrastructure first, Linux-shaped through 1.50:** IRQ, sched, mm, VFS/block,
#     tty, net, timers, SMP, accounting — learn Linux *roles* (drivers/, virtio,
#     irq, mm, netdev) not clone the kernel or glibc. Framebuffer pixels landed
#     in 1.15 as optional HW; **no UI / compositor / Wayland series on the roadmap.**
#   - **Userspace first:** loadable modules / servers over growing the kernel.
#     Kernel keeps thin primitives (IPC, sched, mm, caps, IRQ mint); drivers and
#     FS policy live in userspace (`drivers/`, servers) when possible.
#   - **1.50** = declared 1.x infra teaching milestone (checklist below).
#   - **MAJOR 2.0** = platform integration of that stack (not a desktop OS).
#

